The issue was that `is_coroutine_callable` was returning `False` because the wrapper was not a coroutine function, so it was going to `run_in_threadpool(call, ...)`.
`run_in_threadpool` calls the function and returns the result. If the function returns a coroutine (which it does, because it's an async function wrapped by `@cache` and `@reawaitable`), then `run_in_threadpool` returns that coroutine object.
